        "ratings": [
            {
                "comment": "My favorite class of all 4 years at UW. Jonah knows a ton about Hollywood history. His lectures were enthusiastic and sometimes really funny. The 1st research paper (on movie theaters) was kind of a challenge and he should probably cut down on the reading a little, but the class was still fun, we watched a lot of great movies, and I learned a lot.",
                "difficulty_rating": 3,
                "quality_rating": 5
            },
            {
                "comment": "Challenging and fun instructor. There's a lot of reading but quizzes are open note (and no midterm). Lectures are really interesting and easy to stay engaged in.",
